      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "*Heart of Darkness* follows Charles Marlow as he travels up the Congo River to investigate the horrifying activities of a trading company. He witnesses the brutal exploitation and dehumanization of the indigenous Congolese people by the European colonizers. A central theme is the corruption of European civilization when confronted with the \"darkness\" of imperial ambition. Specifically, the book depicts the Congolese not as fully developed individuals, but often as primitive objects or obstacles in the face of European hypocrisy and greed.",
