      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can counter the \"neutral artifact\" argument by pointing out that colonial language is never truly neutral; it serves ideological functions of control and hierarchy. The terminology used in *Heart of Darkness* is not just a vocabulary of the age but a discursive tool designed to justify exploitation and dehumanize the colonized subject. Therefore, viewing it as \"performing power\" is a critical lens that acknowledges how language itself participates in constructing racial and imperial realities.",
      "source": "target",
